{"context": "published", "host": "www.josephsmithpapers.org", "showHeader": true, "footerStyle": "mini", "statusCode": 200, "uri": "report-of-committee-5february-1841", "page": "2", "is404": false, "gallery": [{"image": "/12339/12339_ms16800_2_05_001_thumb.jpg", "page": "1", "label": "[1]", "href": "/paper-summary/report-of-committee-5february-1841/1"}, {"image": "/12339/12339_ms16800_2_05_002_thumb.jpg", "page": "2", "label": "[2]", "href": "/paper-summary/report-of-committee-5february-1841/2"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "report-of-committee-5february-1841", "series": "JSPPA", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPA6", "documentSeriesIdCompiled": "jsppa6-sub-nccr-sub02-410208", "documentSeriesUri": "/the-papers/administrative-records/jsppa6/jsppa6-sub-nccr/jsppa6-sub-nccr-sub02/jsppa6-sub-nccr-sub02-410208", "documentSeriesTitle": "<p>\r\n\tMeeting, 8 February 1841</p>", "editorialPageNumber": "2", "isPageNumberPresent": false, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/54007375/54007375-0002.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> —Submitted</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\">Chairman Joseph Smith</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\">City of <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5899025360836871647\"><a href=\"#5899025360836871647\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"plc12\" place=\"plc12\" title=\"Nauvoo, Illinois\">Nauvoo</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Nauvoo, Illinois\"><p>Principal gathering place for Saints following expulsion from Missouri. Beginning in 1839, Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints purchased lands in earlier settlement of Commerce and planned settlement of Commerce City, as well as surrounding areas....</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/nauvoo-illinois\">More Info</a></div></div></aside>. Feby 5. 1841</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\">&nbsp;</div> <div class=\" wasptag\">Report of the Committee on Vacating the Plats of <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"9562737002359474685\"><a href=\"#9562737002359474685\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"plc32\" place=\"plc32\" title=\"Commerce, Illinois\">Commerce</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Commerce, Illinois\"><p>Located near middle of western boundary of state, bordering Mississippi River. European Americans settled area, 1820s. From bank of river, several feet above high-water mark, ground described as nearly level for six or seven blocks before gradually sloping...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/commerce-illinois\">More Info</a></div></div></aside> &amp; <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"2928004298980416067\"><a href=\"#2928004298980416067\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"plc32\" place=\"plc32\" title=\"Commerce, Illinois\">Commerce City</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Commerce, Illinois\"><p>Located near middle of western boundary of state, bordering Mississippi River. European Americans settled area, 1820s. From bank of river, several feet above high-water mark, ground described as nearly level for six or seven blocks before gradually sloping...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/commerce-illinois\">More Info</a></div></div></aside>.</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16762752486774366610\"><a href=\"#16762752486774366610\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans2\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/robert-blashel-thompson\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Robert&nbsp;B. Thompson</a> handwriting ends; JS begins. JS signed his own name and wrote the other names here.</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\">J Smith Char </span>[<span class=\"josephswriting\">Chairman</span>]</div><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6402550370394373450\"><a href=\"#6402550370394373450\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per106\" person=\"per106\" title=\"Wilson Law\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">W</span><span class=\"josephswriting\">ilson</span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> Law</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Law, Wilson\"><p>26 Feb. 1806–15 Oct. 1876. Merchant, millwright, land speculator, farmer. Born in Ireland. Son of Richard Law and Ann Hunter. Immigrated to U.S. and settled in Springfield Township, Mercer Co., Pennsylvania, by 1820. Moved to Delaware Township, Mercer Co....</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/wilson-law\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside></div><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10069022623459657159\"><a href=\"#10069022623459657159\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per983\" person=\"per983\" title=\"Charles Coulson Rich\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">C</span><span class=\"josephswriting\">harles&nbsp;C.</span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> Rich</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Rich, Charles Coulson\"><p>21 Aug. 1809–17 Nov. 1883. Schoolteacher, farmer, cooper. Born in Campbell Co., Kentucky. Son of Joseph Rich and Nancy O’Neal. Moved to Posey Township, Dearborn Co., Indiana, ca. 1810. Moved to Tazewell Co., Illinois, 1829. Baptized into Church of Jesus Christ...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/charles-coulson-rich\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span> [p. [2]]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> —Submitted</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\">Chairman Joseph Smith</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\">City of <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"4827123891461395742\"><a href=\"#4827123891461395742\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"plc12\" place=\"plc12\" title=\"Nauvoo, Illinois\">Nauvoo</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Nauvoo, Illinois\"><p>Principal gathering place for Saints following expulsion from Missouri. Beginning in 1839, Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints purchased lands in earlier settlement of Commerce and planned settlement of Commerce City, as well as surrounding areas....</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/nauvoo-illinois\">More Info</a></div></div></aside>. Feby 5. 1841</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\">&nbsp;</div> <div class=\" wasptag\">Report of the Committee <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>on <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>Vacating the <span class=\"deleted\">Tow</span> Plats <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>of <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"17852527910418087667\"><a href=\"#17852527910418087667\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"plc32\" place=\"plc32\" title=\"Commerce, Illinois\">Commerce</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Commerce, Illinois\"><p>Located near middle of western boundary of state, bordering Mississippi River. European Americans settled area, 1820s. From bank of river, several feet above high-water mark, ground described as nearly level for six or seven blocks before gradually sloping...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/commerce-illinois\">More Info</a></div></div></aside> &amp; <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"4739461879453836734\"><a href=\"#4739461879453836734\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"plc32\" place=\"plc32\" title=\"Commerce, Illinois\">Commerce <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>City</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Commerce, Illinois\"><p>Located near middle of western boundary of state, bordering Mississippi River. European Americans settled area, 1820s. From bank of river, several feet above high-water mark, ground described as nearly level for six or seven blocks before gradually sloping...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/commerce-illinois\">More Info</a></div></div></aside>.</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"15601316690452234274\"><a href=\"#15601316690452234274\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans2\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/robert-blashel-thompson\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Robert&nbsp;B. Thompson</a> handwriting ends; JS begins. JS signed his own name and wrote the other names here.</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\">J Smith Char </span>[<span class=\"josephswriting\">Chairman</span>]</div><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"9622928869711952938\"><a href=\"#9622928869711952938\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per106\" person=\"per106\" title=\"Wilson Law\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">W</span>[<span class=\"josephswriting\">ilson</span>]<span class=\"josephswriting\"> Law</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidd